> Module Cdcc

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R
> Using Filers as F
> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as QR
> Using Dependents_benefit_split as B

# Child and dependent care credit: IRC 21, IRC 129, Form 2441

Direct File ("DF" below) module `cdcc.xml` (4,152 lines) under
`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/`, with the
per-person facts of `familyAndHousehold.xml` and `filers.xml` and the earned
income facts of `income.xml`. Issue #28, scope.md section 6.3. Law:
`sources/statute/irc-21.html`, `irc-129.html`, `sources/regs/cfr-1.21-1.xml`
to `-3.xml`, `sources/forms-instructions/f2441--2024.pdf` and
`i2441--2024.pdf`, `sources/pubs/p503--2024.pdf`.

Two scopes follow Form 2441. `Form2441PartIII` (Part III, dependent care
benefits, lines 12 to 31) needs no AGI; its output `taxable_benefits` is Form
1040 line 1e. `Form2441` adds Part II (lines 3 to 11) and takes the AGI and the
tax liability limit as inputs. Both take the same household inputs, so the
caller runs `Form2441PartIII` first to fill the Form 1040 slot
`taxable_dependent_care` (line 1e), then `Form2441` once the AGI is known.

Inputs are complete (CONVENTIONS section 3). Wiring (not done here): see the
PR body.

Not modelled, each a knockout (`unsupported`): Worksheet A prior-year
expenses, household employees, benefits from a sole proprietorship or
partnership, both spouses claiming deemed student/disabled income in the same
return, and a taxable-benefit split DF itself refuses. The care provider list
of Part I does not change any amount; its effect (no credit for payments to a
spouse, a parent of the child, a dependent or a child under 19, IRC 21(e)(6))
is carried by the answer `expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider`.

Divergences from DF, all statute-first (CONVENTIONS section 8):

- `DF-BUG(23)`: DF lets a non-parent (a grandparent or foster parent) take
  CDCC for a child through the Form 8332 benefit split. IRC 21(e)(5) gives
  the child to the custodial parent only. Status: candidate. Changes
  `hoh-cdcc-multiple-careproviders`.
- `DF-BUG(24)`: DF gives a 0 decimal amount when AGI is zero or less; the
  statute gives 35 percent.
- `DF-BUG(25)`: DF tests "a qualifying person lived with you" and "you paid
  over half the upkeep" on two possibly different persons for the married
  filing separately exception; IRC 21(e)(4) is about one household.
  Candidate.
- `DF-BUG(26)`: DF takes the spouse's earned income on line 19 for a
  qualifying surviving spouse (it reads the empty secondary filer, so line 19
  is $0). The form says "All others, enter the amount from line 18".
- `DF-BUG(27)`: DF ignores forfeited amounts (line 14) unless box 10 of a
  W-2 is positive; line 14 covers amounts on line 13 as well. Candidate.
- `DF-BUG(28)`: DF requires the filer to have chosen to claim a dependent
  child; IRC 21(b)(1)(A) and i2441 p 1 ask whether the child "can" be
  claimed. Candidate.

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## The `Writable` answers DF keeps per household member that only the CDCC
## reads (`familyAndHousehold.xml`).
declaration structure CdccAnswers:
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/unableToCareForSelf
  data unable_to_care_for_self content boolean
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccHasDependentCareExpenses
  data has_dependent_care_expenses content boolean
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccHadExpensesPaidToQualifyingProvider
  data expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider content boolean
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/writableCdccQualifyingExpenseAmount
  data writable_qualifying_expense_amount content money
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/tpPaidMostOfHomeUpkeep
  data tp_paid_most_of_home_upkeep content boolean

## One member of DF /familyAndHousehold.
declaration structure CdccMember:
  data member content QR.Member
  data cdcc content CdccAnswers

## The per-filer inputs (primary or secondary filer).
declaration structure CdccFiler:
  # DF: income.xml /primaryFilerEmployerIncomeSubtotalBase
  # (Form 1040 lines 1a to 1d, 1f to 1h of this filer, without line 1e)
  data employer_income_subtotal_base content money
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerCombatPay (box 12 code Q)
  data nontaxable_combat_pay content money
  # Form 2441 instructions, lines 4 and 5: the election to include
  # nontaxable combat pay in earned income for the credit
  data elect_combat_pay_for_credit content boolean
  # i2441 p 5, line 18: the same election for Part III
  data elect_combat_pay_for_benefits content boolean
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerDependentCareBenefits (box 10, unrounded sum)
  data dependent_care_benefits content money
  # DF: /writablePrimaryFilerDependentCarePlanMaximum
  data dependent_care_plan_maximum content money
  # DF: /filers/*/isDisabled (physically or mentally incapable of self care)
  data is_disabled content boolean
  # IRC 21(d)(2): one element per calendar month in which this filer was
  # incapable of self care or a full-time student (a student needs at least
  # five such months, IRC 21(e)(7)); the element is the filer's actual earned
  # income in that month. Empty if none. No DF fact (DF knocks these out).
  data deemed_income_month_earnings content list of money
  # DF: /filers/*/cdccHasDependentCareExpenses (only if disabled)
  data has_dependent_care_expenses content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/cdccHadExpensesPaidToQualifyingProvider
  data expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider content boolean
  # DF: /filers/*/writableCdccQualifyingExpenseAmount
  data writable_qualifying_expense_amount content money

## IRC 21(d)(2): the amount by which the deemed income of the listed months
## exceeds the actual income, summed. Each month counts the higher of the
## deemed amount and the actual income (i2441 p 4).
declaration deemed_income_uplift content money
  depends on
    months content list of money,
    deemed content money
  equals
    Money.sum of (map each a among months to Money.positive of (deemed - a))
```

## One person: qualifying person

IRC 21(b)(1): "The term "qualifying individual" means— (A) a dependent of the
taxpayer (as defined in section 152(a)(1)) who has not attained age 13, (B) a
dependent of the taxpayer (as defined in section 152, determined without
regard to subsections (b)(1), (b)(2), and (d)(1)(B)) who is physically or
mentally incapable of caring for himself or herself and who has the same
principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such
taxable year, or (C) the spouse of the taxpayer, if the spouse is physically
or mentally incapable of caring for himself or herself and who has the same
principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such
taxable year."

i2441 p 1: "1. A qualifying child under age 13 whom you can claim as a
dependent. If the child turned 13 during the year, the child is a qualifying
person for the part of the year they were under age 13." "3. Any disabled
person who wasn't physically or mentally able to care for themselves who lived
with you for more than half of the year and whom you can claim as a dependent
or could claim as a dependent except: a. The disabled person had gross income
of $5,050 or more, b. The disabled person filed a joint return, or c. You (or
your spouse if filing jointly) could be claimed as a dependent on another
taxpayer's 2024 tax return."

IRC 21(e)(10): "No credit shall be allowed under this section with respect to
any qualifying individual unless the TIN of such individual is included on the
return claiming the credit." (`Qualifying_relative` requires a TIN of every
eligible dependent.)

IRC 21(e)(5): "If— (A) section 152(e) applies to any child with respect to
any calendar year, and (B) such child is under the age of 13 or is physically
or mentally incapable of caring for himself, ... such child shall be treated
as a qualifying individual described in subparagraph (A) or (B) of subsection
(b)(1) (whichever is appropriate) with respect to the custodial parent (as
defined in section 152(e)(4)(A)), and shall not be treated as a qualifying
individual with respect to the noncustodial parent." i2441 p 1: "Even if you
can't claim your child as a dependent, they are treated as your qualifying
person if: ... You were the child's custodial parent."

DF `/familyAndHousehold/*/cdccQualifyingPerson` (line 1170) and
`cdccNonDependentQualifyingPerson` (line 867) follow the same three paths. DF
also gives the credit to a non-parent who reaches the Form 8332 benefit split
(`tpCanClaimSplitBenefitsHohEitcCdcc`, `reachedNonParentalBenefitSplit`). A
grandparent or foster parent is not a "custodial parent" (IRC 152(e)(4)(A):
"the parent having custody"), and the child is not their dependent, so we do
not (`DF-BUG(23)`).

The age in IRC 21(b)(1)(A) is "age 13" and a child who turns 13 during the
year is a qualifying person for the earlier part (i2441 p 1; Pub. 503 p 3).
DF: `cdccTurnedThirteenAfterJanFirst`, age 13 at year end and not born on
January 1.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope CdccPersonTest:
  # One member of DF /familyAndHousehold
  input cdcc_member content CdccMember
  # DF: filers.xml /minimumFilerDateOfBirth (Filers.minimum_filer_date_of_birth)
  input minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date
  # DF: filers.xml /treatFilersAsDependents
  input treat_filers_as_dependents content boolean
  # DF: filers.xml /eitherFilerUSCitizenOrNational
  input either_filer_us_citizen_or_national content boolean
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFJ
  input treat_as_mfj content boolean

  # The dependent tests for the same person (issues #16, #17, #18)
  output dependent content QR.DependentTest
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/isBornOnJanFirst
  output born_on_january_first condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/ageOnJanFirst
  output age_on_january_first content integer
  # The person was under 13 for at least part of the year
  output under_13_for_part_of_year condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccTurnedThirteenAfterJanFirst
  output turned_thirteen_after_january_first condition
  # IRC 21(b)(1)(A)
  output qualifying_child_under_13 condition
  # IRC 21(b)(1)(B)
  output incapable_dependent condition
  # IRC 21(e)(5)
  output custodial_parent_release condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccQualifyingPerson
  output cdcc_qualifying_person condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccHasQualifyingExpenses
  output has_qualifying_expenses condition
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccQualifyingExpenseAmount
  output qualifying_expense_amount content money
  # IRC 21(e)(4), Form 2441 line A: this person's home tests
  output home_tests_for_married_separate condition
```

```catala
scope CdccPersonTest:
  definition dependent equals
    output of QR.DependentTest with {
      -- member: cdcc_member.member
      -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: minimum_filer_date_of_birth
      -- treat_filers_as_dependents: treat_filers_as_dependents
      -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national:
           either_filer_us_citizen_or_national
      -- treat_as_mfj: treat_as_mfj }

  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/isBornOnJanFirst
  rule born_on_january_first under condition
    Date.get_month of cdcc_member.member.person.date_of_birth = 1
    and Date.get_day of cdcc_member.member.person.date_of_birth = 1
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/ageOnJanFirst
  definition age_on_january_first equals
    if born_on_january_first then dependent.qc.age
    else dependent.qc.age - 1

  rule under_13_for_part_of_year under condition
    age_on_january_first < P.cdcc_qualifying_child_age_limit
  consequence fulfilled

  rule turned_thirteen_after_january_first under condition
    under_13_for_part_of_year
    and dependent.qc.age >= P.cdcc_qualifying_child_age_limit
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 21(b)(1)(A); IRC 152(a)(1) (a qualifying child). DF-BUG(28): the
  # statute asks whether the child is the taxpayer's dependent, not whether
  # the taxpayer elected to claim; `eligible_dependent`, not
  # `is_claimed_dependent`. DF: first branch of /cdccQualifyingPerson.
  rule qualifying_child_under_13 under condition
    dependent.eligible_dependent
    and dependent.qualifying_child
    and under_13_for_part_of_year
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 21(b)(1)(B): a dependent "determined without regard to subsections
  # (b)(1), (b)(2), and (d)(1)(B)" of section 152 (dependent of another,
  # joint return, gross income), incapable of self care, same abode for more
  # than half the year. DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccNonDependentQualifyingPerson,
  # third branch, and the second branch of /cdccQualifyingPerson. A child
  # whom IRC 152(e) assigns to another parent, or who is the benefit-split
  # child (handled below), is not this filer's dependent.
  rule incapable_dependent under condition
    cdcc_member.cdcc.unable_to_care_for_self
    and dependent.qc.residency_test
    and dependent.citizen_or_resident_test
    and cdcc_member.member.answers.tin_type != QR.TinType.NoTin
    and ((dependent.qc.qc_relationship_test and dependent.qc.age_test
          and dependent.qc.qc_support_test)
         or (dependent.not_qualifying_child_test
             and dependent.relationship_member_of_household_test
             and dependent.qr_support_test))
    and not dependent.split.disqualified_due_to_parental_custody
    and not dependent.split.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 21(e)(5): the custodial parent who released the claim keeps the
  # credit. The parent path of DF /tpCanClaimSplitBenefitsHohEitcCdcc
  # (`tp_is_parent`); the non-parent path is DF-BUG(23).
  rule custodial_parent_release under condition
    dependent.split.tp_can_claim_split_benefits_hoh_eitc_cdcc
    and dependent.split.tp_is_parent
    and dependent.citizen_or_resident_test
    and cdcc_member.member.answers.tin_type != QR.TinType.NoTin
    and ((dependent.qualifying_child and under_13_for_part_of_year)
         or (dependent.qc.residency_test
             and cdcc_member.cdcc.unable_to_care_for_self))
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccQualifyingPerson
  rule cdcc_qualifying_person under condition
    qualifying_child_under_13 or incapable_dependent or custodial_parent_release
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccHasQualifyingExpenses
  rule has_qualifying_expenses under condition
    cdcc_member.cdcc.has_dependent_care_expenses
    and cdcc_member.cdcc.expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider
  consequence fulfilled

  # Form 2441 line 2 column (d). DF: /familyAndHousehold/*/cdccQualifyingExpenseAmount
  definition qualifying_expense_amount equals
    if cdcc_qualifying_person and has_qualifying_expenses
    then R.round_dollar of cdcc_member.cdcc.writable_qualifying_expense_amount
    else $0

  # IRC 21(e)(4)(A)(i)-(ii): the home is this person's abode for more than
  # half the year and the filer pays over half its cost.
  rule home_tests_for_married_separate under condition
    cdcc_qualifying_person
    and dependent.qc.residency_test
    and cdcc_member.cdcc.tp_paid_most_of_home_upkeep
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Part III: dependent care benefits (Form 2441 lines 12 to 31)

IRC 129(a)(2)(A): "The amount which may be excluded under paragraph (1) for
dependent care assistance with respect to dependent care services provided
during a taxable year shall not exceed $5,000 ($2,500 in the case of a
separate return by a married individual)." IRC 129(b)(1): the exclusion "shall
not exceed— (A) in the case of an employee who is not married at the close of
such taxable year, the earned income of such employee for such taxable year,
or (B) ... the lesser of— (i) the earned income of such employee ..., or (ii)
the earned income of the spouse of such employee". IRC 129(b)(2): the
section 21(d)(2) deemed income applies to a student or incapable spouse. IRC
21(c): the dollar limit "shall be reduced by the aggregate amount excludable
from gross income under section 129".

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Form2441PartIII:
  # DF: /filingStatus
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # DF: /familyAndHousehold
  input household content list of CdccMember
  # DF: filers.xml /minimumFilerDateOfBirth
  input minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date
  # DF: filers.xml /treatFilersAsDependents
  input treat_filers_as_dependents content boolean
  # DF: filers.xml /eitherFilerUSCitizenOrNational
  input either_filer_us_citizen_or_national content boolean
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /treatAsMFJ
  input treat_as_mfj content boolean
  # DF: filers.xml /livedApartLastSixMonths (Filers.lived_apart_last_six_months)
  input lived_apart_last_six_months condition
  # DF: filers.xml /livedTogetherAllYearWithSpouse, or /spouseLivedTogetherMonths
  # = livedTogetherMoreThanSixMonths
  input spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year condition
  # DF: /filers (primary and, if any, secondary)
  input primary_filer content CdccFiler
  input secondary_filer content CdccFiler
  # DF: income.xml /hasMfjSpouseEarnedIncome, /writableMfsSpouseEarnedIncome
  input has_mfs_spouse_earned_income condition
  input writable_mfs_spouse_earned_income content money
  # DF: /writableCdccTotalQualifiedDependentCareExpenses (line 16)
  input writable_total_qualified_dependent_care_expenses content money
  # DF: /writableCdccCarryoverAmountFromPriorTaxYear (line 13; $0 if none)
  input writable_carryover_amount content money
  # DF: /writableCdccForfeitedCredits (line 14; $0 if none)
  input writable_forfeited_amount content money
  # DF: /cdccHasCreditForPriorYearExpenses, /cdccClaimedCreditForPriorYearExpenses,
  # /cdccClaimedMaxCreditForPriorTaxYear
  input has_credit_for_prior_year_expenses condition
  input claimed_credit_for_prior_year_expenses condition
  input claimed_max_credit_for_prior_tax_year condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutHouseholdEmployee
  input has_household_employee condition
  # Form 2441 line 22 "Yes"
  input benefits_from_sole_proprietorship_or_partnership condition

  output results content list of CdccPersonTest
  internal is_mfj condition
  internal is_mfs condition
  # DF: /cdccQualifyingNonFilersCount
  output non_filer_qualifying_person_count content integer
  # DF: /filers/*/cdccQualifyingPerson
  output primary_filer_is_qualifying_person condition
  output secondary_filer_is_qualifying_person condition
  # DF: /cdccCountOfQualifyingPersons
  output count_of_qualifying_persons content integer
  # DF: /cdccHasQualifyingPersons
  output has_qualifying_persons condition
  # DF: /mfsButEligibleForCdcc, Form 2441 line A
  output mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc condition
  # IRC 21(e)(2)
  output married_separate_not_allowed condition
  # DF: /cdccUncappedQualifyingExpenses
  output uncapped_qualifying_expenses content money
  # Form 2441 line 27. DF: /cdccQualifyingExpenseCap
  output qualifying_expense_cap content money

  # Form 2441 lines 12 to 15
  output primary_dependent_care_benefits content money
  output secondary_dependent_care_benefits content money
  # DF: /cdccDependentCareBenefitsAmount (line 12)
  output line12_dependent_care_benefits content money
  # DF: /cdccCarryoverAmountFromPriorTaxYear (line 13)
  output line13_carryover content money
  # DF: /cdccForfeitedCredits (line 14)
  output line14_forfeited content money
  # DF: /cdccAdjustedDependentCareBenefitsAmount (line 15)
  output line15_adjusted_benefits content money
  # DF: /hasReportedDependentCareBenefits, /isFillingForm2441PartIII
  output has_reported_primary_benefits condition
  output has_reported_secondary_benefits condition
  output has_reported_carryover condition
  output is_filling_part_iii condition
  # DF: /cdccTotalQualifiedDependentCareExpenses (line 16)
  output line16_expenses content money
  # DF: /cdccLesserOfAdjustBenefitsAndQualifiedExpenses (line 17)
  output line17_lesser content money

  # Deemed income (IRC 21(d)(2)) for each filer, if married filing jointly
  output deemed_monthly_income content money
  output primary_deemed_uplift content money
  output secondary_deemed_uplift content money
  # DF: /cdccEarnedIncomePrimaryFilerLine18 (line 18)
  output line18_earned_income content money
  # DF: /cdccEarnedIncomeLine19 (line 19)
  output line19_earned_income content money
  # DF: /cdccTentativeExclusionAmount (line 20)
  output line20_tentative_exclusion content money
  # DF: /cdccMaximumExclusion
  output maximum_exclusion content money
  # DF: /cdccShouldBeAskedAboutMaxExclusion
  output asked_about_max_exclusion condition
  # DF: /cdccSpecifiedExclusionAmount (line 21)
  output line21_specified_exclusion content money
  # Line 22 (out of scope)
  output line22_sole_proprietorship_benefits content money
  # DF: /cdccExclusionAmountNotFromSoleProprietorshipOrPartnership (line 23)
  output line23 content money
  # DF: /cdccDeductibleBenefitsAmount (line 24)
  output line24_deductible_benefits content money
  # DF: /cdccExcludedBenefitsAmount (line 25)
  output line25_excluded_benefits content money
  # DF: /cdccTaxableBenefits (line 26; Form 1040 line 1e)
  output taxable_benefits content money
  # Line 28, 29, 30, 31. DF: /cdccSumOfDeductibleAndExcludedBenefitsAmount,
  # /cdccNetAllowableAmount, /cdccUncappedQualifyingExpenses,
  # /cdccSmallerOfTotalQualifyingExpensesAmount
  output line28 content money
  output line29_net_allowable content money
  output line31 content money
  # DF: /cdccPotentialCdccIsZeroOrLessDueToExclusionBenefits
  output potential_cdcc_is_zero_due_to_exclusion condition

  # Knockouts
  output ko_knockout_cdcc_worksheet_a condition
  output ko_knockout_household_employee condition
  output ko_sole_proprietorship_benefits condition
  output ko_both_spouses_deemed_income condition
  output unsupported condition
```

```catala
scope Form2441PartIII:
  definition is_mfj equals filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition is_mfs equals
    filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately

  definition results equals
    map each m among household to
      (output of CdccPersonTest with {
         -- cdcc_member: m
         -- minimum_filer_date_of_birth: minimum_filer_date_of_birth
         -- treat_filers_as_dependents: treat_filers_as_dependents
         -- either_filer_us_citizen_or_national:
              either_filer_us_citizen_or_national
         -- treat_as_mfj: treat_as_mfj })

  definition non_filer_qualifying_person_count equals
    number of (list of r among results such that r.cdcc_qualifying_person)

  # IRC 21(b)(1)(C): the spouse, "physically or mentally incapable of caring
  # for himself or herself" with the same abode over half the year. DF
  # applies it to either spouse of a joint return.
  # DF: /filers/*/cdccQualifyingPerson
  rule primary_filer_is_qualifying_person under condition
    primary_filer.is_disabled and treat_as_mfj
    and spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year
  consequence fulfilled
  rule secondary_filer_is_qualifying_person under condition
    secondary_filer.is_disabled and treat_as_mfj
    and spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year
  consequence fulfilled

  definition count_of_qualifying_persons equals
    non_filer_qualifying_person_count
    + (if primary_filer_is_qualifying_person then 1 else 0)
    + (if secondary_filer_is_qualifying_person then 1 else 0)

  rule has_qualifying_persons under condition count_of_qualifying_persons > 0
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 21(e)(4), Form 2441 line A. See DF-BUG(25): one person must pass
  # both home tests.
  # DF: filers.xml /mfsButEligibleForCdcc
  rule mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc under condition
    is_mfs and lived_apart_last_six_months
    and exists r among results such that r.home_tests_for_married_separate
  consequence fulfilled

  # IRC 21(e)(2): "If the taxpayer is married at the close of the taxable
  # year, the credit shall be allowed under subsection (a) only if the
  # taxpayer and his spouse file a joint return."
  rule married_separate_not_allowed under condition
    is_mfs and not mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /cdccUncappedQualifyingExpenses (line 30 in Part III)
  definition uncapped_qualifying_expenses equals
    Money.sum of (map each r among results to r.qualifying_expense_amount)
    + (if primary_filer_is_qualifying_person
          and primary_filer.has_dependent_care_expenses
          and primary_filer.expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider
       then R.round_dollar of primary_filer.writable_qualifying_expense_amount
       else $0)
    + (if secondary_filer_is_qualifying_person
          and secondary_filer.has_dependent_care_expenses
          and secondary_filer.expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider
       then R.round_dollar of secondary_filer.writable_qualifying_expense_amount
       else $0)

  # IRC 21(c)(1)-(2). DF: /cdccQualifyingExpenseCap
  definition qualifying_expense_cap equals
    if count_of_qualifying_persons > 1 then P.cdcc_expense_cap_two_or_more
    else if count_of_qualifying_persons = 1 then P.cdcc_expense_cap_one_person
    else $0
```

### Lines 12 to 15

Form 2441 line 12: "Enter the total amount of dependent care benefits you
received in 2024. Amounts you received as an employee should be shown in box
10 of your Form(s) W-2." Line 13: the amount carried over from 2023 and used
in 2024. Line 14: "If you forfeited or carried over to 2025 any of the
amounts reported on line 12 or 13, enter the amount." Line 15: "Combine lines
12 through 14." DF rounds each (`Round`). `DF-BUG(27)`: DF counts a
forfeited amount only if box 10 is positive.

```catala
scope Form2441PartIII:
  definition primary_dependent_care_benefits equals
    primary_filer.dependent_care_benefits
  definition secondary_dependent_care_benefits equals
    if is_mfj then secondary_filer.dependent_care_benefits else $0

  # DF: /hasReportedPrimaryFilerDependentCareBenefits (unrounded sum > 0)
  rule has_reported_primary_benefits under condition
    primary_dependent_care_benefits > $0
  consequence fulfilled
  rule has_reported_secondary_benefits under condition
    secondary_dependent_care_benefits > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /cdccDependentCareBenefitsAmount
  definition line12_dependent_care_benefits equals
    R.round_dollar of primary_dependent_care_benefits
    + (if is_mfj
       then R.round_dollar of secondary_dependent_care_benefits else $0)

  definition line13_carryover equals
    R.round_dollar of writable_carryover_amount

  rule has_reported_carryover under condition line13_carryover > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF-BUG(27)
  definition line14_forfeited equals
    R.round_dollar of writable_forfeited_amount

  # DF: /cdccAdjustedDependentCareBenefitsAmount
  definition line15_adjusted_benefits equals
    line12_dependent_care_benefits + line13_carryover - line14_forfeited

  # DF: /hasReportedDependentCareBenefits and /isFillingForm2441PartIII
  rule is_filling_part_iii under condition
    has_reported_primary_benefits or has_reported_secondary_benefits
    or has_reported_carryover
  consequence fulfilled

  # Line 16. DF: /cdccTotalQualifiedDependentCareExpenses
  definition line16_expenses equals
    if has_qualifying_persons
    then R.round_dollar of writable_total_qualified_dependent_care_expenses
    else $0

  # Line 17. DF: /cdccLesserOfAdjustBenefitsAndQualifiedExpenses
  definition line17_lesser equals
    Money.min of line15_adjusted_benefits, line16_expenses
```

### Lines 18 to 21: earned income and the exclusion limit

i2441 p 5, line 18: "Earned income for figuring the amount of dependent care
benefits you are able to exclude or deduct from your income is determined in
the same way as earned income for figuring the credit is determined ...;
however, for purposes of lines 18 and 19, earned income doesn't include any
dependent care benefits shown on line 12." Line 19: "If your filing status is
married filing separately ... Are you considered unmarried under that rule?
Yes. Enter your earned income (from line 18) on line 19. No. Enter your
spouse's earned income on line 19." The form for all others: "enter the amount
from line 18" (`DF-BUG(26)`).

Earned income of a student or incapable spouse: IRC 21(d)(2) quoted above; Reg.
1.21-2(b)(4)(iii): "Earned income may be attributed under this paragraph
(b)(4), in the case of any husband and wife, to only one spouse in any month."
We apply the rule only to a married filing jointly return (the statute says
"a spouse") and make a return where both spouses list deemed months
unsupported.

```catala
scope Form2441PartIII:
  # IRC 21(d)(2)(A)-(B)
  definition deemed_monthly_income equals
    if count_of_qualifying_persons > 1
    then P.cdcc_deemed_monthly_income_two_or_more
    else if count_of_qualifying_persons = 1
    then P.cdcc_deemed_monthly_income_one_person
    else $0

  definition primary_deemed_uplift equals
    if is_mfj
    then deemed_income_uplift of primary_filer.deemed_income_month_earnings,
                                 deemed_monthly_income
    else $0
  definition secondary_deemed_uplift equals
    if is_mfj
    then deemed_income_uplift of secondary_filer.deemed_income_month_earnings,
                                 deemed_monthly_income
    else $0

  # DF: /cdccEarnedIncomePrimaryFilerLine18
  definition line18_earned_income equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (primary_filer.employer_income_subtotal_base
       + (if primary_filer.elect_combat_pay_for_benefits
          then primary_filer.nontaxable_combat_pay else $0)
       + primary_deemed_uplift)

  # DF: /cdccEarnedIncomeLine19 and /cdccEarnedIncomeSecondaryFilerPartIII
  definition line19_earned_income equals
    if is_mfj
    then R.round_dollar of
      (secondary_filer.employer_income_subtotal_base
       + (if secondary_filer.elect_combat_pay_for_benefits
          then secondary_filer.nontaxable_combat_pay else $0)
       + secondary_deemed_uplift)
    else if married_separate_not_allowed
    then (if has_mfs_spouse_earned_income
          then R.round_dollar of writable_mfs_spouse_earned_income else $0)
    else line18_earned_income

  # Line 20. DF: /cdccTentativeExclusionAmount
  definition line20_tentative_exclusion equals
    if line17_lesser > $0
    then Money.min of line17_lesser,
           (Money.min of line18_earned_income, line19_earned_income)
    else $0

  # IRC 129(a)(2)(A). DF: /cdccMaximumExclusion
  definition maximum_exclusion equals
    if married_separate_not_allowed
    then P.dependent_care_exclusion_cap_married_separate
    else P.dependent_care_exclusion_cap

  # DF: /cdccShouldBeAskedAboutMaxExclusion
  rule asked_about_max_exclusion under condition
    is_filling_part_iii and has_qualifying_persons
  consequence fulfilled

  # Line 21. DF: /cdccSpecifiedExclusionAmount (the plan maxima are read only
  # for a filer who has benefits, /cdccPrimaryFilerDependentCarePlanMaximum)
  definition line21_specified_exclusion equals
    if not asked_about_max_exclusion then $0
    else if (is_mfj or is_mfs) and not mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc
    then Money.min of maximum_exclusion,
      ((if has_reported_primary_benefits or has_reported_carryover
        then R.round_dollar of primary_filer.dependent_care_plan_maximum
        else $0)
       + (if has_reported_secondary_benefits
          then R.round_dollar of secondary_filer.dependent_care_plan_maximum
          else $0))
    else Money.min of maximum_exclusion,
      (if has_reported_primary_benefits or has_reported_carryover
       then R.round_dollar of primary_filer.dependent_care_plan_maximum
       else $0)

  # OUT OF SCOPE: line 22, benefits from a sole proprietorship or
  # partnership; the filer is sent away by ko_sole_proprietorship_benefits.
  definition line22_sole_proprietorship_benefits equals $0

  definition line23 equals line15_adjusted_benefits - line22_sole_proprietorship_benefits

  # Line 24. DF: /cdccDeductibleBenefitsAmount
  definition line24_deductible_benefits equals
    Money.min of line20_tentative_exclusion,
      (Money.min of line21_specified_exclusion,
                    line22_sole_proprietorship_benefits)

  # Line 25, the "No" branch of line 22. DF: /cdccExcludedBenefitsAmount
  definition line25_excluded_benefits equals
    Money.min of line21_specified_exclusion, line20_tentative_exclusion

  # Line 26. DF: /cdccTaxableBenefits
  definition taxable_benefits equals
    if is_filling_part_iii
    then Money.positive of (line23 - line25_excluded_benefits)
    else $0
```

### Lines 27 to 31

Line 27: "Enter $3,000 ($6,000 if two or more qualifying persons)". Line 28: "Add
lines 24 and 25." Line 29: "Subtract line 28 from line 27. If zero or less,
stop. You can't take the credit." Line 30: "Complete line 2 on page 1 of
this form. Don't include in column (d) any benefits shown on line 28 above.
Then, add the amounts in column (d) and enter the total here." Line 31:
"Enter the smaller of line 29 or 30."

```catala
scope Form2441PartIII:
  definition line28 equals line24_deductible_benefits + line25_excluded_benefits
  definition line29_net_allowable equals qualifying_expense_cap - line28
  definition line31 equals Money.min of line29_net_allowable, uncapped_qualifying_expenses

  rule potential_cdcc_is_zero_due_to_exclusion under condition
    is_filling_part_iii and line29_net_allowable <= $0
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Knockouts

```catala
scope Form2441PartIII:
  # DF: /knockoutCdccWorksheetA (flow.xml line 116)
  rule ko_knockout_cdcc_worksheet_a under condition
    has_credit_for_prior_year_expenses
    and (not claimed_credit_for_prior_year_expenses
         or not claimed_max_credit_for_prior_tax_year)
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /flowKnockoutHouseholdEmployee (flow.xml line 117)
  rule ko_knockout_household_employee under condition has_household_employee
  consequence fulfilled

  rule ko_sole_proprietorship_benefits under condition
    benefits_from_sole_proprietorship_or_partnership
  consequence fulfilled

  # Reg. 1.21-2(b)(4)(iii): deemed income for one spouse per month. We cannot
  # check the months, so a return with deemed months for both is refused.
  rule ko_both_spouses_deemed_income under condition
    is_mfj
    and (exists a among primary_filer.deemed_income_month_earnings such that true)
    and (exists b among secondary_filer.deemed_income_month_earnings such that true)
  consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_knockout_cdcc_worksheet_a or ko_knockout_household_employee
    or ko_sole_proprietorship_benefits or ko_both_spouses_deemed_income
  consequence fulfilled
```

## Part II: the credit (Form 2441 lines 3 to 11)

IRC 21(a)(1): "there shall be allowed as a credit against the tax imposed by
this chapter for the taxable year an amount equal to the applicable
percentage of the employment-related expenses ... paid by such individual
during the taxable year." IRC 21(a)(2): "the term "applicable percentage"
means 35 percent reduced (but not below 20 percent) by 1 percentage point for
each $2,000 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross
income for the taxable year exceeds $15,000." IRC 21(d)(1): the expenses
"shall not exceed— (A) in the case of an individual who is not married at the
close of such year, such individual's earned income for such year, or (B) in
the case of an individual who is married at the close of such year, the
lesser of such individual's earned income or the earned income of his spouse".
Form 2441: line 3 "Add the amounts in column (d) of line 2. Don't enter more
than $3,000 if you had one qualifying person or $6,000 if you had two or more
persons. If you completed Part III, enter the amount from line 31." Line 6
"Enter the smallest of line 3, 4, or 5." Line 7 AGI; line 8 the decimal
amount; line 9a "Multiply line 6 by the decimal amount on line 8"; line 10
"Tax liability limit"; line 11 "Enter the smaller of line 9c or line 10".

Earned income (i2441 p 3, lines 4 and 5): "The amount shown on Form 1040,
1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 1z" and "Nontaxable combat pay if you elect to
include it in earned income", each spouse separately, so line 1e (taxable
dependent care benefits) is part of one spouse's earned income. The form does
not say whose; DF allocates the amount below.

`DF-BUG(24)`: AGI zero or less gives 35 percent here; DF gives 0.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Form2441:
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  input household content list of CdccMember
  input minimum_filer_date_of_birth content date
  input treat_filers_as_dependents content boolean
  input either_filer_us_citizen_or_national content boolean
  input treat_as_mfj content boolean
  input lived_apart_last_six_months condition
  input spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year condition
  input primary_filer content CdccFiler
  input secondary_filer content CdccFiler
  input has_mfs_spouse_earned_income condition
  input writable_mfs_spouse_earned_income content money
  input writable_total_qualified_dependent_care_expenses content money
  input writable_carryover_amount content money
  input writable_forfeited_amount content money
  input has_credit_for_prior_year_expenses condition
  input claimed_credit_for_prior_year_expenses condition
  input claimed_max_credit_for_prior_tax_year condition
  input has_household_employee condition
  input benefits_from_sole_proprietorship_or_partnership condition
  # Form 2441 line 7: Form 1040 line 11. DF: /agi
  input agi content money
  # Credit Limit Worksheet line 1: Form 1040 line 18. Line 2 (Schedule 3 line 1,
  # foreign tax credit) is $0: DF does not support it. DF: /totalTentativeTax
  input total_tentative_tax content money

  output benefits scope Form2441PartIII

  # Part III results again at the top level (Form 1040 line 1e and the
  # flat list the differential test reads)
  output taxable_benefits content money
  output count_of_qualifying_persons content integer
  output has_qualifying_persons condition
  output has_more_than_three_qualifying_persons condition
  output mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc condition
  output line12_dependent_care_benefits content money
  output line13_carryover content money
  output line14_forfeited content money
  output line15_adjusted_benefits content money
  output line17_lesser content money
  output line20_tentative_exclusion content money
  output line21_specified_exclusion content money
  output line24_deductible_benefits content money
  output line25_excluded_benefits content money
  output line28 content money
  output line29_net_allowable content money
  output line31 content money

  # Line 3. DF: /cdccQualifyingExpenses
  output line3 content money
  # DF: income.xml /cdccPrimaryEarnedIncomeWithCombatPayForCredits
  output primary_earned_income_before_benefits content money
  output secondary_earned_income_before_benefits content money
  # Allocation of taxable benefits (QUIRK, see below)
  output primary_adjustment content money
  output secondary_adjustment content money
  output allocate_all_to_primary condition
  output allocate_all_to_secondary condition
  output primary_taxable_benefits content money
  output secondary_taxable_benefits content money
  # DF: /cdccEarnedIncomePrimaryFilerLine4 (line 4)
  output line4_earned_income content money
  # DF: /cdccEarnedIncomeLine5 (line 5)
  output line5_earned_income content money
  # DF: /lowerOfCdccEarnedIncome
  output lower_of_earned_income content money
  # DF: /cdccLowerOfEarnedIncomeAndExpenses (line 6)
  output line6 content money
  # Line 8. DF: /xmlCdccCareExpensesDecimalAmount
  output applicable_percentage content decimal
  output line8_decimal_amount content money
  # DF: /cdccTentativeExpenseAmount (line 9a)
  output line9a content money
  # DF: /cdccCreditForPriorYearExpenses (line 9b; out of scope)
  output line9b content money
  # DF: /cdccTotalEligibleCDCCAmount (line 9c)
  output line9c content money
  # DF: /cdccCreditLimit (line 10)
  output line10_tax_liability_limit content money
  # DF: /cdccHasQualifyingExpenses
  output has_qualifying_expenses condition
  # DF: /cdccTotalCredit (line 11; Schedule 3 line 2)
  output cdcc_total_credit content money
  # DF: /isReceivingCdccCredit
  output is_receiving_cdcc_credit condition
  # DF: /shouldSubmitForm2441
  output should_submit_form_2441 condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutBenefitsDistribution
  output ko_flow_knockout_benefits_distribution condition
  output unsupported condition
```

```catala
scope Form2441:
  definition benefits.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition benefits.household equals household
  definition benefits.minimum_filer_date_of_birth equals
    minimum_filer_date_of_birth
  definition benefits.treat_filers_as_dependents equals treat_filers_as_dependents
  definition benefits.either_filer_us_citizen_or_national equals
    either_filer_us_citizen_or_national
  definition benefits.treat_as_mfj equals treat_as_mfj
  definition benefits.lived_apart_last_six_months equals lived_apart_last_six_months
  definition benefits.spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year equals
    spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year
  definition benefits.primary_filer equals primary_filer
  definition benefits.secondary_filer equals secondary_filer
  definition benefits.has_mfs_spouse_earned_income equals has_mfs_spouse_earned_income
  definition benefits.writable_mfs_spouse_earned_income equals
    writable_mfs_spouse_earned_income
  definition benefits.writable_total_qualified_dependent_care_expenses equals
    writable_total_qualified_dependent_care_expenses
  definition benefits.writable_carryover_amount equals writable_carryover_amount
  definition benefits.writable_forfeited_amount equals writable_forfeited_amount
  definition benefits.has_credit_for_prior_year_expenses equals
    has_credit_for_prior_year_expenses
  definition benefits.claimed_credit_for_prior_year_expenses equals
    claimed_credit_for_prior_year_expenses
  definition benefits.claimed_max_credit_for_prior_tax_year equals
    claimed_max_credit_for_prior_tax_year
  definition benefits.has_household_employee equals has_household_employee
  definition benefits.benefits_from_sole_proprietorship_or_partnership equals
    benefits_from_sole_proprietorship_or_partnership

  definition taxable_benefits equals benefits.taxable_benefits
  definition count_of_qualifying_persons equals
    benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons
  rule has_qualifying_persons under condition benefits.has_qualifying_persons
  consequence fulfilled
  rule has_more_than_three_qualifying_persons under condition
    benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons > 3
  consequence fulfilled
  rule mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc under condition
    benefits.mfs_but_eligible_for_cdcc
  consequence fulfilled
  definition line12_dependent_care_benefits equals
    benefits.line12_dependent_care_benefits
  definition line13_carryover equals benefits.line13_carryover
  definition line14_forfeited equals benefits.line14_forfeited
  definition line15_adjusted_benefits equals benefits.line15_adjusted_benefits
  definition line17_lesser equals benefits.line17_lesser
  definition line20_tentative_exclusion equals benefits.line20_tentative_exclusion
  definition line21_specified_exclusion equals benefits.line21_specified_exclusion
  definition line24_deductible_benefits equals benefits.line24_deductible_benefits
  definition line25_excluded_benefits equals benefits.line25_excluded_benefits
  definition line28 equals benefits.line28
  definition line29_net_allowable equals benefits.line29_net_allowable
  definition line31 equals benefits.line31

  # Line 3. DF: /cdccQualifyingExpenses
  definition line3 equals
    if benefits.is_filling_part_iii then benefits.line31
    else Money.min of benefits.uncapped_qualifying_expenses,
                      benefits.qualifying_expense_cap

  rule has_qualifying_expenses under condition
    benefits.uncapped_qualifying_expenses > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: income.xml /cdccPrimaryEarnedIncomeWithCombatPayForCredits
  definition primary_earned_income_before_benefits equals
    primary_filer.employer_income_subtotal_base
    + (if primary_filer.elect_combat_pay_for_credit
       then primary_filer.nontaxable_combat_pay else $0)
    + benefits.primary_deemed_uplift
  definition secondary_earned_income_before_benefits equals
    if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
    then secondary_filer.employer_income_subtotal_base
         + (if secondary_filer.elect_combat_pay_for_credit
            then secondary_filer.nontaxable_combat_pay else $0)
         + benefits.secondary_deemed_uplift
    else $0
```

### Whose earned income holds the taxable benefits

Line 26 is one amount for the return; Form 2441 does not say which spouse's
earned income it adds to. DF chooses so as to give the larger credit, with
the rule below, and knocks the return out when the best choice would need a
calculation it does not do. The statute is silent, so it is reproduced.

```catala
scope Form2441:
  # DF: income.xml /cdccPrimaryFilerMaximumEarnedIncomeAdjustmentFromTaxableBenefits
  definition primary_adjustment equals
    Money.min of benefits.taxable_benefits, benefits.primary_dependent_care_benefits
  definition secondary_adjustment equals
    Money.min of benefits.taxable_benefits, benefits.secondary_dependent_care_benefits

  # QUIRK(Q12): proposed, new. DF /cdccAllTaxableDependentCareBenefitsShouldBeAddedtoPrimaryEarnedIncome
  # compares the other spouse's earned income MINUS this spouse's (the
  # "ToMatch" fact) with this spouse's earned income PLUS the adjustment in its
  # second alternative, which looks like a slip. Reproduced; the allocation is
  # not a rule of law.
  rule allocate_all_to_primary under condition
    benefits.has_reported_primary_benefits
    and (not (filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
              and benefits.has_reported_secondary_benefits)
         or (secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
             - primary_earned_income_before_benefits
             >= primary_earned_income_before_benefits + primary_adjustment)
         or (primary_earned_income_before_benefits
             <= secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
             and (Money.min of secondary_earned_income_before_benefits,
                    (primary_earned_income_before_benefits + primary_adjustment))
                 >= benefits.line31
             and not (secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
                      < primary_earned_income_before_benefits
                        + primary_adjustment)))
  consequence fulfilled

  rule allocate_all_to_secondary under condition
    benefits.has_reported_secondary_benefits
    and (not benefits.has_reported_primary_benefits
         or (primary_earned_income_before_benefits
             - secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
             >= secondary_earned_income_before_benefits + secondary_adjustment)
         or (secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
             < primary_earned_income_before_benefits
             and (Money.min of primary_earned_income_before_benefits,
                    (secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
                     + secondary_adjustment))
                 >= benefits.line31
             and not (primary_earned_income_before_benefits
                      < secondary_earned_income_before_benefits
                        + secondary_adjustment)))
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: income.xml /cdccPrimaryFilerTaxableBenefits
  definition primary_taxable_benefits equals
    if allocate_all_to_primary then primary_adjustment
    else if benefits.taxable_benefits > secondary_adjustment
    then Money.min of primary_adjustment,
                      (benefits.taxable_benefits - secondary_adjustment)
    else $0
  definition secondary_taxable_benefits equals
    if allocate_all_to_secondary then secondary_adjustment
    else if benefits.taxable_benefits > primary_adjustment
    then Money.min of secondary_adjustment,
                      (benefits.taxable_benefits - primary_adjustment)
    else $0

  # Line 4. DF: /cdccEarnedIncomePrimaryFilerLine4
  definition line4_earned_income equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (primary_earned_income_before_benefits + primary_taxable_benefits)
  # Line 5. DF: /cdccEarnedIncomeLine5
  definition line5_earned_income equals
    if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
    then R.round_dollar of
      (secondary_earned_income_before_benefits + secondary_taxable_benefits)
    else line4_earned_income

  # DF: /lowerOfCdccEarnedIncome
  definition lower_of_earned_income equals
    if filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
    then Money.min of line4_earned_income, line5_earned_income
    else line4_earned_income

  # Line 6. DF: /cdccLowerOfEarnedIncomeAndExpenses
  definition line6 equals Money.min of line3, lower_of_earned_income

  # DF: /flowKnockoutBenefitsDistribution (flow.xml line 115)
  rule ko_flow_knockout_benefits_distribution under condition
    filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
    and (benefits.has_reported_carryover
         or (benefits.has_reported_primary_benefits
             and benefits.has_reported_secondary_benefits))
    and benefits.taxable_benefits > $0
    and (primary_earned_income_before_benefits < benefits.line31
         or secondary_earned_income_before_benefits < benefits.line31)
    and not (allocate_all_to_primary or allocate_all_to_secondary)
  consequence fulfilled
```

### Lines 7 to 11

Line 8's table (f2441--2024.pdf p 1): ".35" for AGI up to $15,000, ".34" over
$15,000 to $17,000, and so on by .01 per $2,000, ".20" over $43,000. It is
IRC 21(a)(2) read as "(or fraction thereof)": one point for each started
$2,000 over $15,000.

```catala
scope Form2441:
  # IRC 21(a)(2). DF: /cdccCareExpensesDecimalAmount (DF-BUG(24) at AGI <= 0)
  definition applicable_percentage equals
    if agi <= P.cdcc_percentage_reduction_threshold
    then P.cdcc_maximum_percentage
    else
      let steps equals
        (agi - P.cdcc_percentage_reduction_threshold)
        / P.cdcc_percentage_step_income
      in
      let whole_steps equals Decimal.truncate of steps in
      let started_steps equals
        if steps > whole_steps then whole_steps + 1.0 else whole_steps
      in
      let reduced equals
        P.cdcc_maximum_percentage - P.cdcc_percentage_step * started_steps
      in
      if reduced < P.cdcc_minimum_percentage
      then P.cdcc_minimum_percentage else reduced

  # For the oracle, which holds the decimal amount as a Dollar
  definition line8_decimal_amount equals $1 * applicable_percentage

  # Line 9a. DF: /cdccTentativeExpenseAmount
  definition line9a equals R.round_dollar of (line6 * applicable_percentage)

  # OUT OF SCOPE: line 9b, Worksheet A (ko_knockout_cdcc_worksheet_a unless the
  # filer already claimed the maximum, when the worksheet gives $0).
  definition line9b equals $0

  definition line9c equals line9a + line9b

  # Credit Limit Worksheet line 3. DF: /cdccCreditLimit
  definition line10_tax_liability_limit equals total_tentative_tax

  # Line 11; IRC 21(e)(2), IRC 26. DF: /cdccTotalCredit
  definition cdcc_total_credit equals
    if not benefits.potential_cdcc_is_zero_due_to_exclusion
       and not benefits.married_separate_not_allowed
       and has_qualifying_expenses
       and line6 > $0
    then Money.min of line9c, (Money.positive of line10_tax_liability_limit)
    else $0

  rule is_receiving_cdcc_credit under condition cdcc_total_credit > $0
  consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /shouldSubmitForm2441
  rule should_submit_form_2441 under condition
    is_receiving_cdcc_credit or benefits.is_filling_part_iii
  consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition
    benefits.unsupported or ko_flow_knockout_benefits_distribution
  consequence fulfilled
```
